# Build-time metadata that belongs in the repository, never in the image.
#
# Today's Dockerfile copies named files rather than the whole context, so
# nothing here is currently reachable. This exists so that a later `COPY . .`
# cannot quietly bake the scanner's accepted-CVE list into a published layer,
# where it would advertise exactly which known findings this image ships with.
.trivyignore.yaml
.trivyignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
